  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "The child is mapped as the recipient of the doctor's instruction",
  "description": "The text 'doctor: take this medicine after food' is juxtaposed with the visual of the African child, who is portrayed as the one receiving the instruction. The child's distressed expression and tear are used to imply that he is incapable or foolish for not following the instruction, creating an analogical mapping where the child is the subject of the textual command. This mapping reinforces the stereotype that Black children are cognitively deficient and require constant supervision.",
